
==============================================================================
 B6  known-grain simulation through the lattice reader
==============================================================================
Simulates integer counts with KNOWN grain weights at the NHANES cigarette sample
size, pushes them through the same heap_lattice reader, and compares recovered
weights and forward-predicted round-number shares against the truth. If the
shortfall reproduces, the attenuation explanation becomes evidence.

base counts: resampled from 1019 real NHANES reports.

quantity               true  recovered      ratio
grain 1               0.410      0.407      0.992
grain 5               0.180      0.284      1.579
grain 10              0.120      0.182      1.517
grain 20              0.160      0.127      0.794
residual share        0.130      0.407      3.128

Forward check on the simulated data, where the truth IS known:
  observed share multiple of  5 : 0.768
  observed share multiple of 10 : 0.598
  observed share multiple of 20 : 0.355

The paper reports implied 0.47 / 0.32 / 0.19 against observed 0.57 / 0.43 / 0.22,
a uniform shortfall of 14 to 26 percent. Compare the ratios above.

